@startuml
title D3 — Agent Submission Lifecycle
caption High-level flow from application start through underwriting response

left to right direction

skinparam shadowing false
skinparam linetype ortho
skinparam defaultTextAlignment center
skinparam wrapWidth 200
skinparam maxMessageSize 110
skinparam nodesep 72
skinparam ranksep 82
skinparam padding 18

skinparam rectangle {
  RoundCorner 14
  BorderThickness 1.4
}
skinparam diamond {
  BackgroundColor #FFF8D6
  BorderColor #C8A84E
}

rectangle "1. Start Submission\n\nRetail agent selects the\ninsurance program and begins\na new application." as Start #EAF2FF

rectangle "2. Enter Risk Information\n\nApplicant, locations,\nexposures, coverage needs\nand prior-loss details." as Enter #EAF2FF

rectangle "3. Upload Documents\n\nApplications, loss runs,\nphotos, financials and other\nrequired supporting files." as Upload #EAF2FF

rectangle "4. Portal Validation\n\nRequired fields, formats,\nconditional questions and\ndocument completeness." as Validate #F3F8E8

diamond "Submission\ncomplete?" as Complete

rectangle "5. Correct Submission\n\nAgent fixes missing,\ninvalid or inconsistent\ninformation." as Correct #FFF1DF

rectangle "6. Create Submission\n\nSurefyre assigns an ID,\nrecords submitted status and\ncreates the work item." as Create #F3F8E8

rectangle "7. Route to Underwriting\n\nProgram rules determine\nqueue, assignment, eligibility\nand referral indicators." as Route #F3F8E8

rectangle "8. Underwriting Review\n\nUnderwriter reviews risk,\ndocuments, guidelines,\nauthority and rating." as Review #EAF2FF

diamond "More information\nrequired?" as MoreInfo

rectangle "9. Request Information\n\nUnderwriter sends questions\nor document requests back\nto the retail agent." as Request #FFF1DF

rectangle "10. Respond to Request\n\nAgent supplies missing\ninformation or updated\ndocuments." as Respond #EAF2FF

rectangle "11. Underwriting Outcome\n\nQuote, referral, decline,\nor other status is recorded\nand returned to the portal." as Outcome #EAF2FF

' Main lifecycle row
Start -right-> Enter
Enter -right-> Upload
Upload -right-> Validate
Validate -right-> Complete

Complete -right-> Create : Yes
Create -right-> Route
Route -right-> Review
Review -right-> MoreInfo
MoreInfo -right-> Outcome : No

' Correction loop beneath validation
Complete -down-> Correct : No
Correct -left-> Validate : Revalidate

' Information-request loop beneath underwriting
MoreInfo -down-> Request : Yes
Request -right-> Respond
Respond -up-> Review : Re-review

' Hidden links stabilize the intended row order
Start -[hidden]right-> Enter
Enter -[hidden]right-> Upload
Upload -[hidden]right-> Validate
Validate -[hidden]right-> Complete
Complete -[hidden]right-> Create
Create -[hidden]right-> Route
Route -[hidden]right-> Review
Review -[hidden]right-> MoreInfo
MoreInfo -[hidden]right-> Outcome

legend bottom
|= Area |= Meaning |
| Blue | Agent or underwriting user activity |
| Green | Surefyre validation, workflow and routing |
| Orange | Exception or correction activity |
endlegend

note bottom
This diagram intentionally stops at the first underwriting outcome.
Quote acceptance, bind, policy issuance and renewal are covered
in later insurance-domain and underwriting lifecycle material.
end note

@enduml
